+Its first causal fault is not established by the corrected LiDAR trajectory.
+Neither trajectory is certified as a stair-control localization authority.
+
+## Gravity, prediction, and observation validity
+
+`imu_calibration_path` supplies FAST-LIO YAML `mapping/extrinsic_R`, defined as
+LiDAR-to-IMU rotation. Its inverse rotates IMU vectors into LiDAR axes. The initial
+up vector is the median acceleration in a +/-0.5 second sensor-header window.
+This is an offline initialization with lookahead, requiring a low-dynamic window;
+it does not prove that the robot was stationary. No dominant scene plane defines
+up, so a large wall cannot be selected as the floor.
+
+Gyro integration predicts rotation between the last accepted LiDAR observation
+and the current header stamp. GICP corrects that prediction using geometry. There
+is no wheel input, translational IMU integration, gyro bias estimation, point
+deskew, or extrinsic translation compensation. Fixed YAML extrinsics also do not
+reproduce FAST-LIO's online extrinsic estimation. Existing GICP thresholds remain
+unchanged; the correction is now measured relative to the predicted pose.
+
+`/lidar_registration/status` is a JSON `std_msgs/String` at every selected scan:
+
+- `BOOTSTRAP`: gravity initialization, not a geometric match yet.
+- `TRACKED`: a geometric update passed the existing fitness/innovation checks.
+- `PREDICTED`: gyro supports a short rejected interval; no measured pose is emitted.
+- `LOST`: no accepted current observation outside that diagnostic prediction interval.
+- `WAITING_FOR_INITIALIZATION`: initial LiDAR/IMU support is insufficient.
+
+Fields include `measurement_valid`, `geometry_valid`, `last_valid_stamp_ns`, `measurement_age_s`,
+`prediction_source`, `reason`, fitness, and translation/rotation innovations.
+The CSV retains its original columns and adds these diagnostics; rejected pose
+columns are NaN. `measurement_valid` also includes BOOTSTRAP's initial relative
+pose; consumers requiring a successful scan match must use `geometry_valid`.
+A rejected scan writes no odometry, no transformed points, and
+no map update. Empty live-cloud/path payloads represent the missing observation.
+The live path restarts at the next accepted observation instead of bridging the
+unknown segment. The full global map keeps accepted scans and retains the last
+accepted timestamp even if the recording ends with a tracking loss.
+
+An IMU gap disables gyro prediction for the affected interval. Local geometric
+recovery still starts from the last observation with the same correction limits;
+success is labeled `prediction_source=last_observation`. Once a supported interval
+is available, gyro prediction resumes. Large ambiguous gaps may remain LOST;
+the tool does not invent a global relocalization. `imu_max_gap_s` (0.03) and
+`prediction_display_horizon_s` (0.5) are offline support/diagnostic settings,
+not robot-wide stop rules. Acceptance is not physical position accuracy.
+
+`/lidar_registration/metadata` records the actual calibration-file hash and applied
+rotation. The deprecated `floor_plane_threshold_m` field is accepted for old
+specs but is unused. Regenerate old output bags before using the updated RViz
+labels; historical bags keep their original algorithm and do not gain status data.
